EditCommandMoveRegionCommand.description:
Moves a region (audio, MIDI, pattern, or a take folder) in time, and to another track of a kind that can hold it
when `trackId` is given. `deleteRegions` and `copyRegions` also take every kind;
`splitRegion` takes audio and MIDI.

Pattern.description:
A Step Sequencer pattern: its rows; `swing` 0…1 delays every even 16th (the second, fourth … of each beat)
by `swing` × half a 16th; `seed` seeds the deterministic generator that draws chance and random steps;
`stepTicks` is the rows' step length (240, a 16th, unless set).

TransformMode.description:
What applying a set does: `selectOnly` selects the matching events in the editor and changes nothing (the
editor runs it itself; the `transform` command refuses it); `operateOnly` changes the matching events;
`selectAndOperate` changes them and leaves them selected.
